<PageLayout title="Editorial standards" kicker="How we work" description="How Tech Talk with TimX reports, edits, corrects and handles sponsorship.">
  <p>Readers trust us to tell builders' stories honestly. These are the standards we hold ourselves to.</p>
  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>Nobody pays to be featured. Sponsors and advertisers have no say over which stories we publish or what they say. Sponsored content is always clearly labelled as such.</p>
  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>Stories are based on interviews with the people involved. Where we state facts such as revenue, funding or user numbers, they come from the subject, public records or other reliable sources, and we say which.</p>
  <h2>Fairness</h2>
  <p>Subjects may review quotes for accuracy, but final editorial decisions rest with us. Where a story involves criticism of a third party, we give them a fair chance to respond.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>When we get something wrong, we fix it promptly and note the correction at the end of the story. To report an error, email <a href="mailto:hello@techtalkwithtimx.com">hello@techtalkwithtimx.com</a>.</p>
  <h2>Conflicts of interest</h2>
  <p>If anyone involved in a story has a financial or personal relationship with its subject, we disclose it in the story.</p>
</PageLayout>
